  "pr_bound": true,
  "purpose_context": "On Windows the file system reports fixed modes, so planners that compare the observed mode with a planned POSIX mode plan a chmod that never takes effect: the startup skill sync and upgrade --dry-run report the same phantom repairs forever, while doctor says the project is clean. This Mission makes one host-aware mode comparison the only way planners decide mode equality and adds an architectural gate that keeps it that way (#4927, #4810).",
  "purpose_tldr": "A converged Windows project stops re-planning file-mode repairs it can never apply, on every CLI start and every upgrade preview.",
